        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "96f842e2-a62c-58cb-8fc5-fe67558e626b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Toyota Innova, Toyota Hilux, Toyota Land Cruiser, Fortuner SUV\n- Companies: Toyota\n- Projects: IMV program\n- Events: Toyota War\n- Places: North America, Chad, Libya\n\nFacts:\n- The Toyota Hilux is a series of light commercial vehicles produced and marketed by Toyota.\n- Most countries used the Hilux name for the full life of the series, but in North America Toyota retired the Hilux name in 1976 in favor of \"Truck,\" \"Pickup Truck,\" or \"Compact Truck.\"\n- The Toyota Innova is part of Toyota's IMV program together with the Hilux pickup truck and the Fortuner SUV.\n- The Toyota War takes its name from the Toyota pickup trucks used by Chadian troops, primarily the Toyota Hilux and the Toyota Land Cruiser, in fighting against Libyan forces.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0e3c2ba0-30d4-587e-a857-aa1bed0f3522",
        "text": "Page: Toyota Innova. Sentence: The Innova is part of Toyota's IMV program together with the Hilux pickup truck and the Fortuner SUV.\nPage: Toyota Hilux. Sentence: The Toyota Hilux (also stylized as HiLux and historically as Hi-Lux) is a series of light commercial vehicles produced and marketed by the Japanese manufacturer Toyota.\nPage: Toyota Hilux. Sentence: Most countries used the Hilux name for the entire life of the series but in North America, the Hilux name was retired in 1976 in favor of \"Truck\", \"Pickup Truck\", or \"Compact Truck\".\nPage: Toyota War. Sentence: It takes its name from the Toyota pickup trucks used, primarily the Toyota Hilux and the Toyota Land Cruiser, to provide mobility for the Chadian troops as they fought against the Libyans.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
